# Case 2: TikTok trend clip (948x576, 30 fps, 25.6 s, 15 shots) - one woman in a red kimono, no other people.
# Paths are relative to this folder. Use ${VAR:-default} so command-line values win.
VIDEO=${VIDEO:-input/tiktok_trend.mp4}
CUTS=${CUTS:-35,74,125,169,206,261,287,418,461,480,521,561,703,727}   # PySceneDetect, last cut corrected 728 -> 727
# new character: full_body.jpg + face.jpg -> character sheet (make_char_sheet.py, Qwen-Image-2.1 + Lightning):
# her, dressed in the video's kimono, from 4 angles. All 4 views go to H3 as references. KEEP_OUTFIT=1 keeps the
# kimono of the video. (Face-only variant: FACE_ONLY=1 CHAR_REF=input/face_cutout.png CHAR_REF_EXTRA="")
CHAR_REF=${CHAR_REF:-input/sheet/view_front.png}
CHAR_REF_EXTRA=${CHAR_REF_EXTRA-input/sheet/view_front_left.png input/sheet/view_left.png input/sheet/view_back.png}
CHAR_DETAILS=${CHAR_DETAILS:-"Female, slim build, oval face, fair skin, dark brown eyes, small nose, soft pink lips, light brown hair with see-through bangs, half tied back, wearing the red kimono with the red-and-white wave pattern, white off-shoulder collar, patterned obi and loose yellow sash from the guide video"}
KEEP_OUTFIT=${KEEP_OUTFIT:-1}
JOB=${JOB:-gen_sheet_seed${SEED:-42}}; OUT=${OUT:-final_sheet_seed${SEED:-42}}
TARGET_FACE=${TARGET_FACE:-input/target_face.jpg}   # the woman, cropped from frame 405
TARGET_TEXT=${TARGET_TEXT:-"the woman with long black hair in the red kimono"}
PROTECT=${PROTECT-}                     # nobody else to keep
PRESENCE=${PRESENCE:-head}              # single person: generate segments where her head is visible (front, side, back); hem/sleeve-only and empty segments stay source
